\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

The following theorem states that continous homothetic preferences are represent
ed by functions that are homogeneous of degree one.
 Observe that no monotonicity condition is required for the existence of
 such a representation.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Theorem*

\series bold
\emph on
(10).
 
\series default
\emph default
