\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is homothetic if and only if it admits a continuous representation 
\begin_inset Formula $u:X\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 that is homogeneous of degree one, i.e., such that for each 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha\in\mathbb{R}_{+}$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $u(\alpha x)=\alpha u(x)$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

