\begin_layout Proof
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $X\equiv\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}$
\end_inset

.
 Define two convergent sequences 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{n}\equiv\{(\frac{1}{n},0)\}_{n=1}^{\infty}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}$
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{n}\begin{array}[t]{c}
\longrightarrow\\
^{n\rightarrow\infty}
\end{array}x=(0,0)$
\end_inset

, and 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{n}\equiv\{(0,1)\}_{n=1}^{\infty}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}$
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{n}\begin{array}[t]{c}
\longrightarrow\\
^{n\rightarrow\infty}
\end{array}y=(0,1)$
\end_inset

 Now, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ n\in\mathbb{N}:x^{n}\succsim_{lex}y^{n}$
\end_inset

, but as 
\begin_inset Formula $n\rightarrow\infty$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $y\succsim_{lex}x$
\end_inset

.
 Therefore, 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim_{lex}$
\end_inset

