 is represented by the function 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}$
\end_inset

 that associates with each 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

 the value
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
m_{p}(x)\equiv{\displaystyle \min_{y\in U(\succsim,x)}}p\cdot y
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 be a monotone and continuous preference on 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

.
 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $p\in\mbox{\mathbb{R}}_{++}^{L}.$
\end_inset

 Consider the function 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}$
\end_inset

 that associates with each 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

 the value
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
m_{p}(x)\equiv{\displaystyle \min_{y\in U(\succsim,x)}}\ p\cdot y
\]

\end_inset

 We will prove 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is represented by 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $(\Rightarrow)$
\end_inset

 Assume 
\begin_inset Formula $x\succsim y$
\end_inset

.
 We want to show that 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}(x)\geq m_{p}(y)$
\end_inset

.
 Let
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
x^{*}\in\ \arg{\displaystyle \min_{z\in U(\succsim,x)}}\ p\cdot z
\]

\end_inset

and
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
y^{*}\in\ \arg{\displaystyle \min_{t\in U(\succsim,y)}}\ p\cdot t
\]

\end_inset

So, we have 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}(x)=p\cdot x^{*}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}(y)=p\cdot y^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 Now, by transitivity, 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{*}\succsim x\succsim y\implies x^{*}\succsim y$
\end_inset

.
 This implies that 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{*}\in U(\succsim,y)$
\end_inset

.
 Thus, by the definition of 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{*}$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{*}\geq p\cdot y^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 Therefore, 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}(x)\geq m_{p}(y)$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $(\Leftarrow)$
\end_inset

 Assume 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}(x)\geq m_{p}(y)$
\end_inset

.
 We want to show that 
\begin_inset Formula $x\succsim y$
\end_inset

.
 Suppose for contradiction 
\begin_inset Formula $\neg(x\succsim y)$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is complete, then 
\begin_inset Formula $y\succsim x$
\end_inset

.
 By the definition of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succ$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $\neg(x\succsim y)\ \wedge\ y\succsim x\iff y\succ x$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is monotone and continuous, then 
\begin_inset Formula $y\succ x\implies y\neq0$
\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 be a monotone and continuous preference on 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

.
 Prove that for each 
\begin_inset Formula $\{x,y\}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $y\succ x$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $y\neq0$
\end_inset

.
 Suppose for contradiction 
\begin_inset Formula $y=0$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $x\geq y$
\end_inset

.
 Define the sequences 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{n}\equiv x+\left(\nicefrac{1}{n},\ldots,\nicefrac{1}{n}\right)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{n}\equiv y=0$
\end_inset

.
 Hence, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ n\in\mathbb{N}:x^{n}\gg y^{n}$
\end_inset

, which implies that 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ n\in\mathbb{N}:x^{n}\succ y^{n}$
\end_inset

 by monotonicity of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

.
 Note, 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{n}\rightarrow x$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{n}\rightarrow y$
\end_inset

 as 
\begin_inset Formula $n\rightarrow\infty$
\end_inset

.
 Thus, by continuity of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $x\succsim y$
\end_inset

.
 But this contradicts 
\begin_inset Formula $y\succ x$
\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula $(\rightarrow\leftarrow)$
\end_inset

.
 Therefore, 
\begin_inset Formula $y\neq0$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_inset

Let
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
x^{*}\in\ \arg{\displaystyle \min_{z\in U(\succsim,x)}}\ p\cdot z
\]

\end_inset

and
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
y^{*}\in\ \arg{\displaystyle \min_{t\in U(\succsim,y)}}\ p\cdot t
\]

\end_inset

By transitivity of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{*}\succsim y\succ0\implies y^{*}\succ0$
\end_inset

.
 So, 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{*}\neq0$
\end_inset

.
 With 
\begin_inset Formula $m_{p}(x)\geq m_{p}(y)$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{*}\geq p\cdot y^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $p\gg0$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{*}\neq0$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot y^{*}>0$
\end_inset

.
 Now, by Corollary 1, 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is continuous on 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

 if and only if 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\in\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $U(\succ,x)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $L(\succ,x)$
\end_inset

 are open.
 By transitivity of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{*}\succsim y\succ x\implies y^{*}\succ x$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $y^{*}\in U(\succ,x)$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $U(\succ,x)$
\end_inset

 is open, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists\ \alpha\in(0,1):\alpha y^{*}\in U(\succ,x)$
\end_inset

.
 Define 
\begin_inset Formula $\tilde{y}\equiv\alpha y^{*}$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $y\neq0$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha\in(0,1)$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\tilde{y}\neq0$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $y\gneq\tilde{y}$
\end_inset

.
 Finally, for 
\begin_inset Formula $p\in\mathbb{R}_{++}^{L}$
\end_inset

, we have 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{*}\geq p\cdot y^{*}>p\cdot\tilde{y}$
\end_inset

, which implies that 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{*}>p\cdot\tilde{y}$
\end_inset

.
 To sum up, 
\begin_inset Formula $\tilde{y}\in U(\succ,x)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $p\cdot x^{*}>p\cdot\tilde{y}$
\end_inset

.
 But this contradicts the fact that
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
x^{*}\in\ \arg{\displaystyle \min_{z\in U(\succsim,x)}}\ p\cdot z
\]

\end_inset

Therefore, 
\begin_inset Formula $x\succsim y$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

